{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540059102,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec37a5001KZuI3Ol0ppQ5r0","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec2647001JTB4ZUE3sRgUX3","type":"tool","id":"call_ebff632f157147068f219184","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540058533,"end":1794540059102}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540059111,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec3901001ZbGCt908m4a9Ww","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec2647001JTB4ZUE3sRgUX3","type":"tool","id":"call_ceda0481c3c64149b59a72b3","tool":"skill","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"id":"sk-doc"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"sk-doc\">\n# Skill: sk-doc\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n\n# Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n\nOne advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n`sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\nIt holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\nThe cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n|------|------------|--------|---------|\n| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n| **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n| **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n| **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n| **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n| **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n| **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n| **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n| **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n| **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n| **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n| **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n| **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n| **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n- Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n- Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n- A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n- The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\nThe `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n`sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\nThe two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\nThe advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\nResolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\nAct on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default.\nAn unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n- **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n- **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n- **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n- **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n- **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n- **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-doc/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n  ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n  mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n  hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n  sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n  sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n  sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n  sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n  sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n  scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n  shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n```\n\nEach packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n\n### Shared backbone\n`shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n- Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n- Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n- Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n\nThe generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\nIt makes zero model calls by default.\n`--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n`validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\nIt prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\nThe `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\nThere are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n- **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n- Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n- Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n- Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n- Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n- Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/source.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","title":"skill","metadata":{"metadata":{"name":"sk-doc","directory":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc","truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<skill_content name=\"sk-doc\">\n# Skill: sk-doc\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n\n# Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n\nOne advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n`sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\nIt holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\nThe cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n|------|------------|--------|---------|\n| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n| **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n| **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n| **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n| **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n| **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n| **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n| **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n| **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n| **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n| **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n| **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n| **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n| **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n- Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n- Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n- A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n- The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\nThe `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n`sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\nThe two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\nThe advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\nResolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\nAct on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default.\nAn unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n- **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n- **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n- **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n- **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n- **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n- **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-doc/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n  ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n  mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n  hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n  sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n  sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n  sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n  sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n  sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n  scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n  shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n```\n\nEach packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n\n### Shared backbone\n`shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n- Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n- Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n- Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n\nThe generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\nIt makes zero model calls by default.\n`--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n`validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\nIt prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\nThe `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\nThere are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n- **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n- Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n- Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n- Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n- Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n- Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal--review-remediation/source.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/2026-09-26--manual-testing-playbook--create-goal/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"id\":\"sk-doc\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540058881,"end":1794540059111}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794540060804,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ec40840016nKfZ5ls7laYCo","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec2647001JTB4ZUE3sRgUX3","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"e707ac0faa4f86c530762e4dfa793464947b4cb2","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":7998,"output":93,"reasoning":87,"cache":{"read":29184,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794540064625,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ec4f71001jqm3iLGSMoJvAE","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec40880019nRzqtjYEjpHzR","type":"step-start","snapshot":"fa79e9b0098759a896ec5aee17c3a774d664f6ed"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540068962,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec5a92001s4tAxKiUE6rbBb","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec40880019nRzqtjYEjpHzR","type":"tool","id":"call_975f9ec16399414ba5c58525","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md, lines 1-522\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n6:   - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n7:   - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n8:   - \"surface router pattern\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 2.4.6.0\n12: router_state: active\n13: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n17: \n18: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: This is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n25: `ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n26: (sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\n27: sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\n28: sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\n29: sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\n30: this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\n31: leaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n32: (`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\n33: and both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\n34: contract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n35: `FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\n36: enumerates the whole hub.\n37: \n38: Routing is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\n39: router picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\n40: emits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n45: \n46: - **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n47:   packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n48:   or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n49:   quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n50:   DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n51:   pass review\"\n52:   requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n53:   reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n54: - **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n55:   a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n56:   index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n57:   slim down\" requests.\n58: - **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n59:   readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n60:   Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n61:   capability\" requests.\n62: - **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n63:   the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n64:   Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n65:   mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n66:   so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n67:   `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n68:   not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n69: - **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n70:   ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n71:   maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n72:   by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n73:   the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n74:   `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n75: - **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n76:   scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n77:   agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n78: - **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n79:   request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n80:   command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n81: - **agent-command leaves.** Both packets' READMEs and templates a request to\n82:   author an agent together with its paired `/create` command loads. Fired only\n83:   by the two paired phrases, \"agent and paired\" and \"paired /create\", which no\n84:   single-artifact request carries. The paired intent stays separate rather than\n85:   being expressed as the union of the two above, because the router keeps only\n86:   intents within one point of the top score: a paired request that also names\n87:   the agent would otherwise drop the command half.\n88: - **diagram and chart leaves belong to the `sk-design` hub.** ASCII flowchart,\n89:   decision-tree and standalone HTML chart authoring is `sk-design-diagram` and\n90:   `sk-design-chart` work, and this router declares no intent for it: `/design:diagram`\n91:   and `/design:chart` are the entry points, so \"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"process diagram\",\n92:   \"create a chart\" and \"plot the data\" reach no key in the two maps below.\n93: - **human-voice leaves** — the scope gate, the scoring method and the Human\n94:   Voice Rules standard a request to apply or score that standard loads. Fired\n95:   by \"hvr / human voice rules / apply human voice / rewrite in human voice /\n96:   make this sound human / sounds ai-generated / remove ai tells\" requests. The\n97:   scope gate is the always-loaded leaf, because deciding what a voice edit may\n98:   touch comes before deciding what to change.\n99: - **playbook leaves** — the manual-testing-playbook README a request to author a\n100:   manual testing playbook loads. Fired by \"playbook system / manual testing\n101:   playbook / testing playbook / playbook scenario / manual test\n102:   scenario\" requests.\n103: - **playbook-conversation leaves** — the conversation-scenario reference and the\n104:   conversation snippet template a request to write a multi-turn json conversation script for\n105:   a playbook scenario loads. Fired by \"playbook conversation / multi-turn\n106:   conversation script / json conversation / conversation runner\" requests. This\n107:   intent scores double. \"manual testing playbook\" also matches \"testing\n108:   playbook\", so that one phrase scores the playbook intent twice, and at equal\n109:   weight a request naming both a playbook and a conversation would load only the\n110:   playbook README. At double weight the two tie and both leaf sets load.\n111: - **feature-catalog leaves** — the feature-catalog README a request to inventory a\n112:   project's features / capabilities loads. Fired by \"feature catalog / feature\n113:   inventory / capabilities\" requests.\n114: - **readme-creation leaves** — the readme README and readme template a request to\n115:   author a project README / front-page overview loads. Fired by \"create a readme /\n116:   readme for / project overview / landing doc\" requests.\n117: - **changelog leaves** — the changelog template a request to author release notes\n118:   / version notes loads. Fired by \"changelog / release notes / what shipped /\n119:   since the last version\" requests.\n120: - **benchmark leaves** — the benchmark shared README, worked example, and report\n121:   template a request to author a behavior benchmark\n122:   loads. Fired by \"create a benchmark / benchmark suite / behavior benchmark\"\n123:   requests.\n124: - **diff leaves** — the diff README, workflow, and worked example a request to\n125:   produce a before/after document diff loads. Fired by \"document diff / before\n126:   and after diff / visual document diff\" requests.\n127: - **repo-rule leaves** — the four decision tests, the rule anatomy contract, the\n128:   creation standards, the wiring contract, the rule and router templates, and the\n129:   packet reference map a\n130:   request to add, change, or remove a repo-local rule loads. Fired by \"repo rule /\n131:   project rule / REPO RULES.md / trigger table / retire a repo rule\" requests. Most such\n132:   requests end in a refusal, so `decision-tests.md` is the always-loaded leaf.\n133: - **frontmatter leaves** — the field reference and the versioning standard a\n134:   request about a frontmatter block itself loads. Fired by \"yaml frontmatter /\n135:   frontmatter block / frontmatter field / description budget / 4-part version /\n136:   frontmatter versioning\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n137:   because `agent frontmatter` belongs to agent-creation and a bare \"frontmatter\"\n138:   would take that route away from it. The field reference is the always-loaded\n139:   leaf, because resolving the document class comes before any field rule.\n140: - **goal-authoring leaves** — the goal authoring standards, the goal exemplars,\n141:   the parent/nested goal workflows and the budget/handoff reference a request to\n142:   author or revise a packet's `goal.md` loads. Fired by \"packet goal / goal.md /\n143:   goal document / author goal.md / phase parent goal / goal criteria /\n144:   completion checks\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n145:   because a bare \"goal\" and the session verbs belong to session-goal management\n146:   (set, bind, update, resend), which the goal hooks and host commands own. The\n147:   authoring standards are the always-loaded leaf, because what a goal must state\n148:   comes before how one is phrased.\n149: - **full-inventory leaves** — the entire sk-doc toolkit. `FULL_INVENTORY` is the\n150:   single explicit full-toolkit intent; no other intent enumerates the whole hub.\n151:   Fired only by an explicit \"show the full sk-doc toolkit / everything sk-doc\n152:   offers\" request.\n153: \n154: A single dominant documentation axis routes to one mode's leaf set; two clearly\n155: separate axes route to both.\n156: \n157: ---\n158: \n159: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n160: \n161: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is the\n162: human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n163: router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the\n164: matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n165: dual-reads to a canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json` or the hub's\n166: `leaf-aliases.json`.\n167: \n168: ```python\n169: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n170:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"documentation quality\", \"doc quality\", \"validate documentation\", \"validate a document\", \"validate this document\", \"validate markdown\", \"validation rules\", \"score this document\", \"score this doc\", \"dqi\", \"document audit\", \"fail sk-doc standards\", \"review the docs\", \"review the documentation\", \"document for clarity\", \"check the docs\", \"check the documentation\", \"audit the docs\", \"documentation review bar\", \"quality bar\", \"flag\", \"meet our standards\", \"audit documentation quality\", \"ai-friendly documentation\", \"extract structure\", \"validate\", \"score\", \"harden\", \"audit\", \"/doc:quality\"]},\n171:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"optimize\", \"token efficiency\", \"llms.txt\", \"llmstxt\", \"reduce tokens\", \"fewer tokens\", \"trim\", \"compress the doc\", \"slim down\", \"model's budget\", \"machine-readable index\", \"optimize this doc\"]},\n172:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"sk-skill\", \"create a new sk\", \"create sk-\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"skill.md and starter\", \"resource_map wiring\", \"new skill\", \"create a skill\", \"build a skill\", \"author a skill\", \"scaffold a skill\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"new capability\", \"capability module\", \"package a capability\", \"create skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"package skill\", \"which json files does a skill need\", \"skill root metadata contract\", \"leaf-manifest config aliases required\", \"/create:skill\"]},\n173:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n174:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"rewrite guard\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n175:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create an agent\", \"create agent\", \"new agent\", \"author an agent\", \"scaffold an agent\", \"agent file\", \"agent persona\", \"agent frontmatter\", \"agent template\", \"permission object\", \"authority boundary\", \"@analyze agent\", \"opencode agent\", \"claude code agent\", \"/create:agent\"]},\n176:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a command\", \"create command\", \"slash command\", \"new slash command\", \"author a command\", \"scaffold a command\", \"argument-hint\", \"allowed-tools\", \"command template\", \"router presentation split\", \"thin router\", \"presentation contract\", \"opencode command\", \"$arguments\", \"/create:command\"]},\n177:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"agent and paired\", \"paired /create\"]},\n178:     \"HVR\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"hvr\", \"human voice rules\", \"apply human voice\", \"rewrite in human voice\", \"make this sound human\", \"sounds ai-generated\", \"reads like ai wrote it\", \"reads like a machine wrote it\", \"remove ai tells\", \"ai writing tells\", \"voice pass\", \"de-ai the writing\", \"banned word check\", \"human voice\"]},\n179:     \"PLAYBOOK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"playbook system\", \"manual testing playbook\", \"testing playbook\", \"deterministic scenario\", \"evidence collection\", \"operator validation\", \"multi-agent execution\", \"release readiness\", \"playbook scenario\", \"manual test scenario\", \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\"]},\n180:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": {\"weight\": 8, \"keywords\": [\"playbook conversation\", \"multi-turn conversation script\", \"json conversation\", \"conversation runner\", \"run-conversation-scenario\"]},\n181:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"feature catalog\", \"feature inventory\", \"catalog of features\", \"features overview\", \"capabilities\", \"catalog package\", \"per-feature files\", \"source anchors\", \"root catalog\", \"capability inventory\", \"/create:feature-catalog\"]},\n182:     \"README_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a readme\", \"readme for\", \"a readme\", \"front-page overview\", \"project overview\", \"getting started doc\", \"intro doc\", \"overview doc\", \"landing doc\", \"create readme\", \"readme\", \"folder readme\", \"write readme\", \"readme.md\", \"code folder readme\", \"/create:readme\"]},\n183:     \"CHANGELOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"changelog\", \"release notes\", \"version notes\", \"release summary\", \"what shipped\", \"since the last version\", \"changelog entry\", \"nested changelog\", \"packet changelog\", \"packet-local changelog\", \"create changelog\", \"global changelog\", \"vx.y.z.b\", \"/create:changelog\"]},\n184:     \"BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a benchmark\", \"author a benchmark\", \"benchmark suite\", \"benchmark authoring\", \"behavior benchmark\", \"benchmark-report.md\", \"source.md\", \"mcp-server/benchmarks\", \"behavior-benchmark.md\", \"scenario contract\", \"claude-baseline\", \"benchmark/readme.md\", \"run-label folder\", \"benchmark package\", \"benchmark fixture\", \"benchmark profile\", \"reviewer-prompt fixture\", \"agent quality dimensions\", \"new benchmark\", \"promote benchmark folder\", \"create benchmark\", \"behavior_benchmark\"]},\n185:     \"DIFF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"document diff\", \"doc diff\", \"diff document\", \"before and after diff\", \"before/after diff\", \"visual document diff\", \"create diff report\", \"document before after review\", \"before after document diff\", \"document change report\", \"before and after document\", \"document before/after review\", \"before/after document diff\", \"review document edits\", \"docx diff\", \"pdf diff\"]},\n186:     \"REPO_RULE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"repo rule\", \"repo-rules\", \"repo rules\", \"project rule\", \"repo rule file\", \"REPO RULES.md\", \"trigger table\", \"rule router\", \"retire a rule\", \"retire a repo rule\", \"revise a rule\", \"revise a repo rule\", \"add a repo rule\", \"always-loaded rule\", \"rule that binds\", \"create repo rule\", \"new repo rule\", \"repo-local rule\", \"we should always\", \"stop doing\", \"add a rule\", \"/create:repo-rule\"]},\n187:     \"FRONTMATTER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"yaml frontmatter\", \"frontmatter block\", \"frontmatter template\", \"frontmatter field\", \"frontmatter fields\", \"trigger_phrases\", \"trigger phrases\", \"importance_tier\", \"contextType\", \"description budget\", \"4-part version\", \"X.Y.Z.W\", \"frontmatter versioning\", \"frontmatter version\", \"version field\", \"frontmatter validation\", \"missing frontmatter\", \"frontmatter contract\", \"yaml header\", \"goes at the top of the file\", \"version number at the top\", \"importance tier\", \"versioning pass\", \"stopped showing up in suggestions\", \"validator says my file is missing\", \"description too long\", \"edit count\", \"field the validator wants\"]},\n188:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create packet goal\", \"packet goal\", \"goal.md\", \"author goal.md\", \"revise packet goal\", \"phase parent goal\", \"nested phase child goal\", \"nested goal\", \"add a goal file\", \"write a goal file\", \"draft a goal file\", \"goal file\", \"goal document\", \"goal criteria\", \"completion checks\", \"measurable criteria\", \"durable objective\", \"phase objective\", \"parent objective\", \"objective for a packet\", \"phase-child goal\", \"child-phase goal\", \"binding table\", \"goal chat slice\", \"/create:goal\"]},\n189:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full sk-doc toolkit\", \"all templates\", \"entire toolkit\", \"everything sk-doc offers\"]},\n190: }\n191: \n192: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n193:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": [\n194:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n195:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n196:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n197:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\"\n198:     ],\n199:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": [\n200:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n201:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\"\n202:     ],\n203:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": [\n204:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n205:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n206:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n207:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\"\n208:     ],\n209:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": [\n210:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n211:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\"\n212:     ],\n213:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n214:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n215:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n216:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n217:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n218:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n219:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\"\n220:     ],\n221:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": [\n222:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n223:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\"\n224:     ],\n225:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": [\n226:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n227:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n228:     ],\n229:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": [\n230:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n231:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n232:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n233:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n234:     ],\n235:     \"HVR\": [\n236:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n237:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n238:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n239:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\"\n240:     ],\n241:     \"PLAYBOOK\": [\n242:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\"\n243:     ],\n244:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": [\n245:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n246:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\"\n247:     ],\n248:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": [\n249:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\"\n250:     ],\n251:     \"README_CREATION\": [\n252:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n253:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\"\n254:     ],\n255:     \"CHANGELOG\": [\n256:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\"\n257:     ],\n258:     \"BENCHMARK\": [\n259:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n260:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n261:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\"\n262:     ],\n263:     \"DIFF\": [\n264:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n265:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n266:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\"\n267:     ],\n268:     \"REPO_RULE\": [\n269:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n270:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n271:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n272:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n273:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n274:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n275:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\"\n276:     ],\n277:     \"FRONTMATTER\": [\n278:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n279:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n280:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\"\n281:     ],\n282:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": [\n283:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n284:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n285:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n286:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n287:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n288:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n289:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\"\n290:     ],\n291:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n292:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n293:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n294:         \"sk-create-agent/references/agent-vs-skill-vs-command.md\",\n295:         \"sk-create-agent/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n296:         \"sk-create-agent/references/permission-design.md\",\n297:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n298:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/over-budget-description.md\",\n299:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/under-budget-trim-lost-tokens.md\",\n300:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n301:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\",\n302:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n303:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n304:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\",\n305:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n306:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n307:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n308:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n309:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n310:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-baseline-template.md\",\n311:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-index-template.md\",\n312:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-scenario-template.md\",\n313:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\",\n314:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/source-template.md\",\n315:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-guide.md\",\n316:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n317:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/case-studies.md\",\n318:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/pitfalls.md\",\n319:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n320:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\",\n321:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/README.md\",\n322:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/topology-edge-cases.md\",\n323:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/version-bump-rules.md\",\n324:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/worked-examples.md\",\n325:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json\",\n326:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.schema.json\",\n327:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-presentation-template.md\",\n328:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-router-template.md\",\n329:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\",\n330:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n331:         \"sk-create-command/references/argument-hints-and-modes.md\",\n332:         \"sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n333:         \"sk-create-command/references/router-presentation-split.md\",\n334:         \"sk-create-command/references/worked-example.md\",\n335:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n336:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-after.md\",\n337:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-before.md\",\n338:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n339:         \"sk-create-diff/references/accessibility-contract.md\",\n340:         \"sk-create-diff/references/capabilities-and-fidelity.md\",\n341:         \"sk-create-diff/references/cli-reference.md\",\n342:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\",\n343:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n344:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-snippet-template.md\",\n345:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-template.md\",\n346:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\",\n347:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n348:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/examples.md\",\n349:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\",\n350:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-snippet-template.md\",\n351:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-template.md\",\n352:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\",\n353:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n354:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n355:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/examples.md\",\n356:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/prompt-voice.md\",\n357:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\",\n358:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n359:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\",\n360:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n361:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/README.md\",\n362:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n363:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/transformation-patterns.md\",\n364:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/validation-and-enforcement.md\",\n365:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflow-examples.md\",\n366:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n367:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/architecture-template.md\",\n368:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-code-template.md\",\n369:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\",\n370:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n371:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/quality-and-checklist.md\",\n372:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/types-and-voice.md\",\n373:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/writing-patterns.md\",\n374:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n375:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n376:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\",\n377:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n378:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n379:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n380:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n381:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n382:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/README.md\",\n383:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\",\n384:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n385:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n386:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-command-metadata-template.json\",\n387:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-description-template.json\",\n388:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n389:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n390:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n391:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-leaf-aliases-template.json\",\n392:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n393:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n394:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\",\n395:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md\",\n396:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md\",\n397:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md\",\n398:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n399:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json\",\n400:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n401:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md\",\n402:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n403:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\",\n404:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md\",\n405:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md\",\n406:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\",\n407:         \"sk-create-skill/references/README.md\",\n408:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md\",\n409:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-lockstep-surfaces.json\",\n410:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n411:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n412:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n413:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n414:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/overview.md\",\n415:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n416:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n417:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n418:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\",\n419:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\"\n420:     ],\n421: }\n422: ```\n423: \n424: ---\n425: \n426: ## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n427: \n428: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n429: - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the\n430:   union is deduped by canonical pair.\n431: - No keyword match is UNKNOWN_FALLBACK: confirm the target artifact and intent\n432:   before loading anything.\n433: - `FULL_INVENTORY` fires only on an explicit \"show the whole toolkit\" request.\n434: - A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.\n435: \n436: ---\n437: \n438: ## 5. MACHINE ROUTER\n439: \n440: The hub's detailed routing prose, moved here from `SKILL.md` so the skill body keeps only a short routing summary and a pointer to this file. It sits last, after the stage-two map above, and it declares no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 stays the only replay source.\n441: \n442: > **Compiled routing (default-on, flag-gated, additive).** Resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n443: > ```bash\n444: > node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"\n445: > ```\n446: > Follow the returned decision — `route` (use its `targets`), `clarify`/`defer` (disambiguate), `reject` (refuse). On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving-authority. Compiled routing is now the default for `sk-doc`; set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide — the explicit kill-switch.\n447: \n448: ### Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n449: \n450: Stage 2 of routing lives in section 3 of this file.\n451: It defines three things:\n452: - The per-intent leaf model: document quality, optimization, skill creation, parent-hub creation, agent creation, command creation, the paired agent-plus-command lane, the human-voice pass, playbooks, playbook conversations, feature catalogs, READMEs, changelogs, benchmarks, diffs, frontmatter, packet goals, repo rules, and the explicit full-toolkit intent.\n453: - The machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP` block that the deterministic router-replay and benchmarks parse.\n454: - The how-to-read rules: a dominant intent gives one leaf set, near-tied intents give a deduped union, and no keyword match gives the hub UNKNOWN fallback, never a silent default.\n455: \n456: Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is packet-qualified or an authored shared-alias disk path, and each converts to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary.\n457: \n458: The reason this file stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` and from `hub-router.json` is in [the parent-skill reference](sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md#why-the-leaf-router-stays-in-routermd).\n459: \n460: ### The discriminator\n461: - **`workflowMode`** — the public packet key (e.g. `sk-create-skill`, `sk-create-quality-control`). `sk-create-skill-parent` is a second mode over the same `sk-create-skill` packet.\n462: - **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for every sk-doc packet (there is no surface axis; the sk-create-quality-control pipeline is universal doctrine in `shared/`, not orthogonal stack-evidence).\n463: - **`backendKind`** — `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators, `sk-create-quality-control` for the sk-create-quality-control mode.\n464: \n465: ### Routing rule\n466: ```\n467: SKILL_ROOT = path containing this ROUTER.md and its SKILL.md\n468: REGISTRY = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n469: HUB_ROUTER = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n470: \n471: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n472:     \"Confirm whether this is sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control work\",\n473:     \"Confirm the target document or component being authored, scaffolded, or reviewed\",\n474:     \"Provide the available inputs: existing doc, source material, or scaffold parameters\",\n475:     \"Confirm the validation expectations before completion (DQI/HVR scoring, validate.sh, or packet-specific checks)\",\n476: ]\n477: \n478: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n479:   resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n480:   resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n481:   if resolved.suffix.lower() not in {\".md\", \".json\"}:\n482:     raise ValueError(\"only skill-local markdown/json router resources are routable\")\n483:   return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n484: \n485: def load_if_available(relative_path, seen):\n486:   guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n487:   if guarded not in seen and (SKILL_ROOT / guarded).exists():\n488:     load(guarded)\n489:     seen.add(guarded)\n490:     return True\n491:   return False\n492: \n493: seen = set()\n494: if not REGISTRY.exists() or not HUB_ROUTER.exists():\n495:   return defer(\"router metadata missing; inspect sk-doc/mode-registry.json and sk-doc/hub-router.json\")\n496: \n497: read mode-registry.json and hub-router.json\n498: classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n499:   (dominant authoring/quality intent; a command like /create:agent resolves directly)\n500: \n501: if confidence is low, intent is contradictory, or routerPolicy.defaultMode is null and no mode wins:\n502:   for resource in hub_router.routerPolicy.defaultResource:   # the ordered defer set, never hardcoded here\n503:     load_if_available(resource, seen)\n504:   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n505: \n506: for each resolved workflowMode:\n507:   entry = the matching mode-registry.json modes[] item\n508:   if entry is missing or entry.packetKind != \"workflow\":\n509:     return defer(\"unknown sk-doc workflowMode; extend mode-registry.json and create a packet first\")\n510:   if not load_if_available(f\"{entry.packet}/SKILL.md\", seen):\n511:     return defer(\"registered packet SKILL.md is missing; repair the packet before routing\")\n512: \n513: return single or orderedBundle according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n514: ```\n515: `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: an unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation rather than forcing a stale default. `hub-router.json` carries the router signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource, and bundle rules. Outcomes are `single`, `orderedBundle`, or `defer` — there is no `surfaceBundle` (no surface axis).\n516: \n517: Per-packet behavior is **not flattened**: each packet keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets, scripts, and templates.\n518: \n519: This hub does **not** use keyed resource discovery (`references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/`) at the hub root.\n520: There are no hub-root `references/` or `assets/` directories, and packet resources stay inside their owning packet or the shared backbone.\n521: If a future workflow needs keyed resource subdirectories, add that behavior inside the owning packet using guarded runtime discovery.\n522: Do not hardcode resource inventories in this hub.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md, lines 1-522\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n6:   - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n7:   - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n8:   - \"surface router pattern\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 2.4.6.0\n12: router_state: active\n13: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n17: \n18: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: This is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n25: `ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n26: (sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\n27: sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\n28: sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\n29: sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\n30: this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\n31: leaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n32: (`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\n33: and both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\n34: contract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n35: `FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\n36: enumerates the whole hub.\n37: \n38: Routing is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\n39: router picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\n40: emits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n45: \n46: - **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n47:   packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n48:   or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n49:   quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n50:   DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n51:   pass review\"\n52:   requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n53:   reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n54: - **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n55:   a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n56:   index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n57:   slim down\" requests.\n58: - **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n59:   readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n60:   Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n61:   capability\" requests.\n62: - **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n63:   the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n64:   Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n65:   mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n66:   so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n67:   `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n68:   not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n69: - **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n70:   ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n71:   maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n72:   by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n73:   the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n74:   `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n75: - **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n76:   scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n77:   agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n78: - **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n79:   request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n80:   command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n81: - **agent-command leaves.** Both packets' READMEs and templates a request to\n82:   author an agent together with its paired `/create` command loads. Fired only\n83:   by the two paired phrases, \"agent and paired\" and \"paired /create\", which no\n84:   single-artifact request carries. The paired intent stays separate rather than\n85:   being expressed as the union of the two above, because the router keeps only\n86:   intents within one point of the top score: a paired request that also names\n87:   the agent would otherwise drop the command half.\n88: - **diagram and chart leaves belong to the `sk-design` hub.** ASCII flowchart,\n89:   decision-tree and standalone HTML chart authoring is `sk-design-diagram` and\n90:   `sk-design-chart` work, and this router declares no intent for it: `/design:diagram`\n91:   and `/design:chart` are the entry points, so \"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"process diagram\",\n92:   \"create a chart\" and \"plot the data\" reach no key in the two maps below.\n93: - **human-voice leaves** — the scope gate, the scoring method and the Human\n94:   Voice Rules standard a request to apply or score that standard loads. Fired\n95:   by \"hvr / human voice rules / apply human voice / rewrite in human voice /\n96:   make this sound human / sounds ai-generated / remove ai tells\" requests. The\n97:   scope gate is the always-loaded leaf, because deciding what a voice edit may\n98:   touch comes before deciding what to change.\n99: - **playbook leaves** — the manual-testing-playbook README a request to author a\n100:   manual testing playbook loads. Fired by \"playbook system / manual testing\n101:   playbook / testing playbook / playbook scenario / manual test\n102:   scenario\" requests.\n103: - **playbook-conversation leaves** — the conversation-scenario reference and the\n104:   conversation snippet template a request to write a multi-turn json conversation script for\n105:   a playbook scenario loads. Fired by \"playbook conversation / multi-turn\n106:   conversation script / json conversation / conversation runner\" requests. This\n107:   intent scores double. \"manual testing playbook\" also matches \"testing\n108:   playbook\", so that one phrase scores the playbook intent twice, and at equal\n109:   weight a request naming both a playbook and a conversation would load only the\n110:   playbook README. At double weight the two tie and both leaf sets load.\n111: - **feature-catalog leaves** — the feature-catalog README a request to inventory a\n112:   project's features / capabilities loads. Fired by \"feature catalog / feature\n113:   inventory / capabilities\" requests.\n114: - **readme-creation leaves** — the readme README and readme template a request to\n115:   author a project README / front-page overview loads. Fired by \"create a readme /\n116:   readme for / project overview / landing doc\" requests.\n117: - **changelog leaves** — the changelog template a request to author release notes\n118:   / version notes loads. Fired by \"changelog / release notes / what shipped /\n119:   since the last version\" requests.\n120: - **benchmark leaves** — the benchmark shared README, worked example, and report\n121:   template a request to author a behavior benchmark\n122:   loads. Fired by \"create a benchmark / benchmark suite / behavior benchmark\"\n123:   requests.\n124: - **diff leaves** — the diff README, workflow, and worked example a request to\n125:   produce a before/after document diff loads. Fired by \"document diff / before\n126:   and after diff / visual document diff\" requests.\n127: - **repo-rule leaves** — the four decision tests, the rule anatomy contract, the\n128:   creation standards, the wiring contract, the rule and router templates, and the\n129:   packet reference map a\n130:   request to add, change, or remove a repo-local rule loads. Fired by \"repo rule /\n131:   project rule / REPO RULES.md / trigger table / retire a repo rule\" requests. Most such\n132:   requests end in a refusal, so `decision-tests.md` is the always-loaded leaf.\n133: - **frontmatter leaves** — the field reference and the versioning standard a\n134:   request about a frontmatter block itself loads. Fired by \"yaml frontmatter /\n135:   frontmatter block / frontmatter field / description budget / 4-part version /\n136:   frontmatter versioning\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n137:   because `agent frontmatter` belongs to agent-creation and a bare \"frontmatter\"\n138:   would take that route away from it. The field reference is the always-loaded\n139:   leaf, because resolving the document class comes before any field rule.\n140: - **goal-authoring leaves** — the goal authoring standards, the goal exemplars,\n141:   the parent/nested goal workflows and the budget/handoff reference a request to\n142:   author or revise a packet's `goal.md` loads. Fired by \"packet goal / goal.md /\n143:   goal document / author goal.md / phase parent goal / goal criteria /\n144:   completion checks\" requests. The phrases are qualified rather than bare,\n145:   because a bare \"goal\" and the session verbs belong to session-goal management\n146:   (set, bind, update, resend), which the goal hooks and host commands own. The\n147:   authoring standards are the always-loaded leaf, because what a goal must state\n148:   comes before how one is phrased.\n149: - **full-inventory leaves** — the entire sk-doc toolkit. `FULL_INVENTORY` is the\n150:   single explicit full-toolkit intent; no other intent enumerates the whole hub.\n151:   Fired only by an explicit \"show the full sk-doc toolkit / everything sk-doc\n152:   offers\" request.\n153: \n154: A single dominant documentation axis routes to one mode's leaf set; two clearly\n155: separate axes route to both.\n156: \n157: ---\n158: \n159: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n160: \n161: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is the\n162: human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n163: router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the\n164: matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n165: dual-reads to a canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json` or the hub's\n166: `leaf-aliases.json`.\n167: \n168: ```python\n169: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n170:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"documentation quality\", \"doc quality\", \"validate documentation\", \"validate a document\", \"validate this document\", \"validate markdown\", \"validation rules\", \"score this document\", \"score this doc\", \"dqi\", \"document audit\", \"fail sk-doc standards\", \"review the docs\", \"review the documentation\", \"document for clarity\", \"check the docs\", \"check the documentation\", \"audit the docs\", \"documentation review bar\", \"quality bar\", \"flag\", \"meet our standards\", \"audit documentation quality\", \"ai-friendly documentation\", \"extract structure\", \"validate\", \"score\", \"harden\", \"audit\", \"/doc:quality\"]},\n171:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"optimize\", \"token efficiency\", \"llms.txt\", \"llmstxt\", \"reduce tokens\", \"fewer tokens\", \"trim\", \"compress the doc\", \"slim down\", \"model's budget\", \"machine-readable index\", \"optimize this doc\"]},\n172:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"sk-skill\", \"create a new sk\", \"create sk-\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"skill.md and starter\", \"resource_map wiring\", \"new skill\", \"create a skill\", \"build a skill\", \"author a skill\", \"scaffold a skill\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"new capability\", \"capability module\", \"package a capability\", \"create skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"package skill\", \"which json files does a skill need\", \"skill root metadata contract\", \"leaf-manifest config aliases required\", \"/create:skill\"]},\n173:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"parent hub\", \"parent skill\", \"mode packet\", \"mode packets\", \"nested packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\", \"hub versus standalone skill class\", \"skill hub\", \"/create:skill-parent\"]},\n174:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"rewrite guard\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n175:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create an agent\", \"create agent\", \"new agent\", \"author an agent\", \"scaffold an agent\", \"agent file\", \"agent persona\", \"agent frontmatter\", \"agent template\", \"permission object\", \"authority boundary\", \"@analyze agent\", \"opencode agent\", \"claude code agent\", \"/create:agent\"]},\n176:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a command\", \"create command\", \"slash command\", \"new slash command\", \"author a command\", \"scaffold a command\", \"argument-hint\", \"allowed-tools\", \"command template\", \"router presentation split\", \"thin router\", \"presentation contract\", \"opencode command\", \"$arguments\", \"/create:command\"]},\n177:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"agent and paired\", \"paired /create\"]},\n178:     \"HVR\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"hvr\", \"human voice rules\", \"apply human voice\", \"rewrite in human voice\", \"make this sound human\", \"sounds ai-generated\", \"reads like ai wrote it\", \"reads like a machine wrote it\", \"remove ai tells\", \"ai writing tells\", \"voice pass\", \"de-ai the writing\", \"banned word check\", \"human voice\"]},\n179:     \"PLAYBOOK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"playbook system\", \"manual testing playbook\", \"testing playbook\", \"deterministic scenario\", \"evidence collection\", \"operator validation\", \"multi-agent execution\", \"release readiness\", \"playbook scenario\", \"manual test scenario\", \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\"]},\n180:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": {\"weight\": 8, \"keywords\": [\"playbook conversation\", \"multi-turn conversation script\", \"json conversation\", \"conversation runner\", \"run-conversation-scenario\"]},\n181:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"feature catalog\", \"feature inventory\", \"catalog of features\", \"features overview\", \"capabilities\", \"catalog package\", \"per-feature files\", \"source anchors\", \"root catalog\", \"capability inventory\", \"/create:feature-catalog\"]},\n182:     \"README_CREATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a readme\", \"readme for\", \"a readme\", \"front-page overview\", \"project overview\", \"getting started doc\", \"intro doc\", \"overview doc\", \"landing doc\", \"create readme\", \"readme\", \"folder readme\", \"write readme\", \"readme.md\", \"code folder readme\", \"/create:readme\"]},\n183:     \"CHANGELOG\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"changelog\", \"release notes\", \"version notes\", \"release summary\", \"what shipped\", \"since the last version\", \"changelog entry\", \"nested changelog\", \"packet changelog\", \"packet-local changelog\", \"create changelog\", \"global changelog\", \"vx.y.z.b\", \"/create:changelog\"]},\n184:     \"BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a benchmark\", \"author a benchmark\", \"benchmark suite\", \"benchmark authoring\", \"behavior benchmark\", \"benchmark-report.md\", \"source.md\", \"mcp-server/benchmarks\", \"behavior-benchmark.md\", \"scenario contract\", \"claude-baseline\", \"benchmark/readme.md\", \"run-label folder\", \"benchmark package\", \"benchmark fixture\", \"benchmark profile\", \"reviewer-prompt fixture\", \"agent quality dimensions\", \"new benchmark\", \"promote benchmark folder\", \"create benchmark\", \"behavior_benchmark\"]},\n185:     \"DIFF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"document diff\", \"doc diff\", \"diff document\", \"before and after diff\", \"before/after diff\", \"visual document diff\", \"create diff report\", \"document before after review\", \"before after document diff\", \"document change report\", \"before and after document\", \"document before/after review\", \"before/after document diff\", \"review document edits\", \"docx diff\", \"pdf diff\"]},\n186:     \"REPO_RULE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"repo rule\", \"repo-rules\", \"repo rules\", \"project rule\", \"repo rule file\", \"REPO RULES.md\", \"trigger table\", \"rule router\", \"retire a rule\", \"retire a repo rule\", \"revise a rule\", \"revise a repo rule\", \"add a repo rule\", \"always-loaded rule\", \"rule that binds\", \"create repo rule\", \"new repo rule\", \"repo-local rule\", \"we should always\", \"stop doing\", \"add a rule\", \"/create:repo-rule\"]},\n187:     \"FRONTMATTER\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"yaml frontmatter\", \"frontmatter block\", \"frontmatter template\", \"frontmatter field\", \"frontmatter fields\", \"trigger_phrases\", \"trigger phrases\", \"importance_tier\", \"contextType\", \"description budget\", \"4-part version\", \"X.Y.Z.W\", \"frontmatter versioning\", \"frontmatter version\", \"version field\", \"frontmatter validation\", \"missing frontmatter\", \"frontmatter contract\", \"yaml header\", \"goes at the top of the file\", \"version number at the top\", \"importance tier\", \"versioning pass\", \"stopped showing up in suggestions\", \"validator says my file is missing\", \"description too long\", \"edit count\", \"field the validator wants\"]},\n188:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create packet goal\", \"packet goal\", \"goal.md\", \"author goal.md\", \"revise packet goal\", \"phase parent goal\", \"nested phase child goal\", \"nested goal\", \"add a goal file\", \"write a goal file\", \"draft a goal file\", \"goal file\", \"goal document\", \"goal criteria\", \"completion checks\", \"measurable criteria\", \"durable objective\", \"phase objective\", \"parent objective\", \"objective for a packet\", \"phase-child goal\", \"child-phase goal\", \"binding table\", \"goal chat slice\", \"/create:goal\"]},\n189:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full sk-doc toolkit\", \"all templates\", \"entire toolkit\", \"everything sk-doc offers\"]},\n190: }\n191: \n192: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n193:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": [\n194:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n195:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n196:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n197:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\"\n198:     ],\n199:     \"OPTIMIZATION\": [\n200:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n201:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\"\n202:     ],\n203:     \"SKILL_CREATION\": [\n204:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n205:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n206:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n207:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\"\n208:     ],\n209:     \"RENDER_LEDGER\": [\n210:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n211:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\"\n212:     ],\n213:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n214:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n215:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n216:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n217:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n218:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n219:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\"\n220:     ],\n221:     \"AGENT_CREATION\": [\n222:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n223:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\"\n224:     ],\n225:     \"COMMAND_CREATION\": [\n226:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n227:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n228:     ],\n229:     \"AGENT_COMMAND\": [\n230:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n231:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n232:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n233:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\"\n234:     ],\n235:     \"HVR\": [\n236:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n237:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n238:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n239:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\"\n240:     ],\n241:     \"PLAYBOOK\": [\n242:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\"\n243:     ],\n244:     \"PLAYBOOK_CONVERSATION\": [\n245:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n246:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\"\n247:     ],\n248:     \"FEATURE_CATALOG\": [\n249:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\"\n250:     ],\n251:     \"README_CREATION\": [\n252:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n253:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\"\n254:     ],\n255:     \"CHANGELOG\": [\n256:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\"\n257:     ],\n258:     \"BENCHMARK\": [\n259:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n260:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n261:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\"\n262:     ],\n263:     \"DIFF\": [\n264:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n265:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n266:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\"\n267:     ],\n268:     \"REPO_RULE\": [\n269:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n270:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n271:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n272:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n273:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n274:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n275:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\"\n276:     ],\n277:     \"FRONTMATTER\": [\n278:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n279:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n280:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\"\n281:     ],\n282:     \"GOAL_AUTHORING\": [\n283:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n284:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n285:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n286:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n287:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n288:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n289:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\"\n290:     ],\n291:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n292:         \"sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md\",\n293:         \"sk-create-agent/references/README.md\",\n294:         \"sk-create-agent/references/agent-vs-skill-vs-command.md\",\n295:         \"sk-create-agent/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n296:         \"sk-create-agent/references/permission-design.md\",\n297:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n298:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/over-budget-description.md\",\n299:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/fixtures/under-budget-trim-lost-tokens.md\",\n300:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md\",\n301:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/README.md\",\n302:         \"sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md\",\n303:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-exemplars.md\",\n304:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-child-template.md\",\n305:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-phase-parent-template.md\",\n306:         \"sk-create-goal/assets/goal-top-level-template.md\",\n307:         \"sk-create-goal/references/authoring-standards.md\",\n308:         \"sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md\",\n309:         \"sk-create-goal/references/parent-and-nested-goals.md\",\n310:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-baseline-template.md\",\n311:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-index-template.md\",\n312:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-scenario-template.md\",\n313:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/benchmark-report-template.md\",\n314:         \"sk-create-benchmark/assets/shared/source-template.md\",\n315:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark-guide.md\",\n316:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\",\n317:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/case-studies.md\",\n318:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/pitfalls.md\",\n319:         \"sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n320:         \"sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md\",\n321:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/README.md\",\n322:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/topology-edge-cases.md\",\n323:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/version-bump-rules.md\",\n324:         \"sk-create-changelog/references/worked-examples.md\",\n325:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json\",\n326:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.schema.json\",\n327:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-presentation-template.md\",\n328:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-router-template.md\",\n329:         \"sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md\",\n330:         \"sk-create-command/references/README.md\",\n331:         \"sk-create-command/references/argument-hints-and-modes.md\",\n332:         \"sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n333:         \"sk-create-command/references/router-presentation-split.md\",\n334:         \"sk-create-command/references/worked-example.md\",\n335:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/README.md\",\n336:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-after.md\",\n337:         \"sk-create-diff/assets/fixtures/onboarding-before.md\",\n338:         \"sk-create-diff/references/README.md\",\n339:         \"sk-create-diff/references/accessibility-contract.md\",\n340:         \"sk-create-diff/references/capabilities-and-fidelity.md\",\n341:         \"sk-create-diff/references/cli-reference.md\",\n342:         \"sk-create-diff/references/worked-example.md\",\n343:         \"sk-create-diff/references/workflow.md\",\n344:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-snippet-template.md\",\n345:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/assets/feature-catalog-template.md\",\n346:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md\",\n347:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n348:         \"sk-create-feature-catalog/references/examples.md\",\n349:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-conversation-snippet-template.md\",\n350:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-snippet-template.md\",\n351:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/assets/manual-testing-playbook-template.md\",\n352:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md\",\n353:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/common-pitfalls.md\",\n354:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/conversation-scenarios.md\",\n355:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/examples.md\",\n356:         \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/prompt-voice.md\",\n357:         \"shared/assets/llmstxt-templates.md\",\n358:         \"shared/references/core-standards.md\",\n359:         \"shared/references/evergreen-packet-id-rule.md\",\n360:         \"shared/references/validation.md\",\n361:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/README.md\",\n362:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/optimization.md\",\n363:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/transformation-patterns.md\",\n364:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/validation-and-enforcement.md\",\n365:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflow-examples.md\",\n366:         \"sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md\",\n367:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/architecture-template.md\",\n368:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-code-template.md\",\n369:         \"sk-create-readme/assets/readme-template.md\",\n370:         \"sk-create-readme/references/README.md\",\n371:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/quality-and-checklist.md\",\n372:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/types-and-voice.md\",\n373:         \"sk-create-readme/references/readme/writing-patterns.md\",\n374:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rule-template.md\",\n375:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/assets/repo-rules-router-template.md\",\n376:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/README.md\",\n377:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/agents-md-integration.md\",\n378:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/creation-standards.md\",\n379:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/decision-tests.md\",\n380:         \"sk-create-repo-rule/references/rule-anatomy.md\",\n381:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/assets/voice-report-template.md\",\n382:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/README.md\",\n383:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md\",\n384:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scope-and-exemptions.md\",\n385:         \"sk-create-with-human-voice/references/scoring-and-verification.md\",\n386:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-command-metadata-template.json\",\n387:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-description-template.json\",\n388:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n389:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\",\n390:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n391:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-leaf-aliases-template.json\",\n392:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n393:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\",\n394:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\",\n395:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md\",\n396:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md\",\n397:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md\",\n398:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-graph-metadata-template.json\",\n399:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json\",\n400:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n401:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md\",\n402:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md\",\n403:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\",\n404:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md\",\n405:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md\",\n406:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\",\n407:         \"sk-create-skill/references/README.md\",\n408:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md\",\n409:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-lockstep-surfaces.json\",\n410:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n411:         \"sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n412:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n413:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n414:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/overview.md\",\n415:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n416:         \"sk-create-skill/references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n417:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n418:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\",\n419:         \"sk-create-skill/references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\"\n420:     ],\n421: }\n422: ```\n423: \n424: ---\n425: \n426: ## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n427: \n428: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n429: - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the\n430:   union is deduped by canonical pair.\n431: - No keyword match is UNKNOWN_FALLBACK: confirm the target artifact and intent\n432:   before loading anything.\n433: - `FULL_INVENTORY` fires only on an explicit \"show the whole toolkit\" request.\n434: - A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.\n435: \n436: ---\n437: \n438: ## 5. MACHINE ROUTER\n439: \n440: The hub's detailed routing prose, moved here from `SKILL.md` so the skill body keeps only a short routing summary and a pointer to this file. It sits last, after the stage-two map above, and it declares no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 stays the only replay source.\n441: \n442: > **Compiled routing (default-on, flag-gated, additive).** Resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n443: > ```bash\n444: > node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"\n445: > ```\n446: > Follow the returned decision — `route` (use its `targets`), `clarify`/`defer` (disambiguate), `reject` (refuse). On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving-authority. Compiled routing is now the default for `sk-doc`; set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide — the explicit kill-switch.\n447: \n448: ### Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n449: \n450: Stage 2 of routing lives in section 3 of this file.\n451: It defines three things:\n452: - The per-intent leaf model: document quality, optimization, skill creation, parent-hub creation, agent creation, command creation, the paired agent-plus-command lane, the human-voice pass, playbooks, playbook conversations, feature catalogs, READMEs, changelogs, benchmarks, diffs, frontmatter, packet goals, repo rules, and the explicit full-toolkit intent.\n453: - The machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP` block that the deterministic router-replay and benchmarks parse.\n454: - The how-to-read rules: a dominant intent gives one leaf set, near-tied intents give a deduped union, and no keyword match gives the hub UNKNOWN fallback, never a silent default.\n455: \n456: Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is packet-qualified or an authored shared-alias disk path, and each converts to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary.\n457: \n458: The reason this file stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` and from `hub-router.json` is in [the parent-skill reference](sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md#why-the-leaf-router-stays-in-routermd).\n459: \n460: ### The discriminator\n461: - **`workflowMode`** — the public packet key (e.g. `sk-create-skill`, `sk-create-quality-control`). `sk-create-skill-parent` is a second mode over the same `sk-create-skill` packet.\n462: - **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for every sk-doc packet (there is no surface axis; the sk-create-quality-control pipeline is universal doctrine in `shared/`, not orthogonal stack-evidence).\n463: - **`backendKind`** — `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators, `sk-create-quality-control` for the sk-create-quality-control mode.\n464: \n465: ### Routing rule\n466: ```\n467: SKILL_ROOT = path containing this ROUTER.md and its SKILL.md\n468: REGISTRY = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n469: HUB_ROUTER = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n470: \n471: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n472:     \"Confirm whether this is sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control work\",\n473:     \"Confirm the target document or component being authored, scaffolded, or reviewed\",\n474:     \"Provide the available inputs: existing doc, source material, or scaffold parameters\",\n475:     \"Confirm the validation expectations before completion (DQI/HVR scoring, validate.sh, or packet-specific checks)\",\n476: ]\n477: \n478: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n479:   resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n480:   resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n481:   if resolved.suffix.lower() not in {\".md\", \".json\"}:\n482:     raise ValueError(\"only skill-local markdown/json router resources are routable\")\n483:   return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n484: \n485: def load_if_available(relative_path, seen):\n486:   guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n487:   if guarded not in seen and (SKILL_ROOT / guarded).exists():\n488:     load(guarded)\n489:     seen.add(guarded)\n490:     return True\n491:   return False\n492: \n493: seen = set()\n494: if not REGISTRY.exists() or not HUB_ROUTER.exists():\n495:   return defer(\"router metadata missing; inspect sk-doc/mode-registry.json and sk-doc/hub-router.json\")\n496: \n497: read mode-registry.json and hub-router.json\n498: classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n499:   (dominant authoring/quality intent; a command like /create:agent resolves directly)\n500: \n501: if confidence is low, intent is contradictory, or routerPolicy.defaultMode is null and no mode wins:\n502:   for resource in hub_router.routerPolicy.defaultResource:   # the ordered defer set, never hardcoded here\n503:     load_if_available(resource, seen)\n504:   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n505: \n506: for each resolved workflowMode:\n507:   entry = the matching mode-registry.json modes[] item\n508:   if entry is missing or entry.packetKind != \"workflow\":\n509:     return defer(\"unknown sk-doc workflowMode; extend mode-registry.json and create a packet first\")\n510:   if not load_if_available(f\"{entry.packet}/SKILL.md\", seen):\n511:     return defer(\"registered packet SKILL.md is missing; repair the packet before routing\")\n512: \n513: return single or orderedBundle according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n514: ```\n515: `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: an unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation rather than forcing a stale default. `hub-router.json` carries the router signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource, and bundle rules. Outcomes are `single`, `orderedBundle`, or `defer` — there is no `surfaceBundle` (no surface axis).\n516: \n517: Per-packet behavior is **not flattened**: each packet keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets, scripts, and templates.\n518: \n519: This hub does **not** use keyed resource discovery (`references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/`) at the hub root.\n520: There are no hub-root `references/` or `assets/` directories, and packet resources stay inside their owning packet or the shared backbone.\n521: If a future workflow needs keyed resource subdirectories, add that behavior inside the owning packet using guarded runtime discovery.\n522: Do not hardcode resource inventories in this hub."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540067474,"end":1794540068962}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540068966,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec5ec60017qIIg5THva7d4X","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec40880019nRzqtjYEjpHzR","type":"tool","id":"call_cb6a8b5ff30b44548b7e8a1a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-236\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n61: What to do when a claim cannot be resolved is\n62: [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](uncertainty-and-honesty.md).\n63: \n64: **A receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it.** If the claim being false would\n65: have left the receipt unchanged, the receipt is not an observation of that claim. It\n66: belongs in INFERRED until repaired. Four shapes recur, each with one repair.\n67: A search that found nothing: demonstrate the search on a known instance of what you claim\n68: is absent, or you have tested your pattern, not the claim. A read that stopped short: read\n69: the span where the failure would actually print. A total carried from another analysis:\n70: derive it here, at the total's own level. A match that never distinguished roles: compare\n71: what the two sides are, not the digits they share. With no known instance to hand, the\n72: honest output is INFERRED plus the step that would confirm it.\n73: \n74: When a report leads with a cause, the cause carries its standing, and the cause-then-fix\n75: order holds. Where no run confirms the cause, it is INFERRED: label it as suspected and\n76: name the next check. A confirmed cause is reported as a finding with its receipt. There\n77: is no unmarked case.\n78: \n79: The failure this prevents: an unconfirmed cause asserted as definitive, which the next\n80: reader treats as settled and stops testing.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 2. COMMAND EVIDENCE\n85: \n86: **A command counts as evidence only after its output and exit status have been read.**\n87: \n88: - Never report output you did not see, or the output you *expected*.\n89: - **Exit 0 with no output is a suspicious pass, not a pass.** A runner that failed to\n90:   start, a script that no-oped on a symlinked path, a matcher that selected zero files,\n91:   and a stale build that refused to run all exit 0 or print nothing.\n92: - **Verify by content, not exit code.** Require the affirmative marker (`RESULT: PASSED`,\n93:   the test count, the file listing), not merely the absence of a failure marker.\n94: - Run focused checks during repair; before claiming completion **re-run the whole\n95:   authoritative gate**. A focused pass is not a gate pass.\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 3. THE FOUR WAYS A GREEN RUN LIES\n100: \n101: 1. **It did not run.** Stale build, refused start, missing binary, guard clause, crashed\n102:    before the first test body.\n103: 2. **It ran on the wrong thing.** Wrong path, branch, or working directory; a symlink\n104:    that resolved elsewhere; a filter that matched nothing. A search that returns nothing\n105:    is not evidence of absence until you have confirmed it read the file: `grep` treats a\n106:    source file holding a NUL byte as binary and prints nothing at all. Re-run with `-a`\n107:    before concluding.\n108: 3. **It ran on stale artifacts.** Cached output, an old bundle, pre-change fixtures, a\n109:    metadata fingerprint that no longer attests its source.\n110: 4. **It asserted nothing.** A test with no assertion, a mocked subject, an auto-updated\n111:    snapshot, an empty parametrization.\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 4. THE NEGATIVE CONTROL\n116: \n117: **Before the fix, reproduce the exact failing symptom with the exact check you will use\n118: to prove the fix.** A check that passed before your change and passes after it proves\n119: nothing about your change. If reproducing is unsafe, say so and name what you used\n120: instead.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 5. BASELINES\n125: \n126: \"No regressions\" is a comparison, and a comparison needs a before.\n127: \n128: 1. Capture the real starting numbers, pass/fail counts, timings, sizes, before\n129:    changing anything.\n130: 2. Re-run the **whole** gate afterwards, not the subset you were iterating on.\n131: 3. Report the delta, including the parts that did not move.\n132: \n133: Same for any performance claim: measure under stated conditions, report baseline and\n134: delta. An unmeasured performance claim is not a caveat, it is a fabrication.\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## 6. SHAPE-SPECIFIC PROOF\n139: \n140: - **Filter or transform:** enumerate every in-scope variant *first*, process each, then\n141:   rescan the whole surface for residue. The variants you never enumerated are the ones\n142:   you missed.\n143: - **Computed answer:** derive it a second way, independently, before writing the number.\n144:   Re-reading your own arithmetic is not an independent derivation.\n145: - **Exact artifact:** check filename, path, format and content shape directly. Having\n146:   written it is not evidence it is there in the required shape.\n147: \n148: ---\n149: \n150: ## 7. A FINDING IS A HYPOTHESIS\n151: \n152: A sub-agent's \"COMPLETE\", a reviewer's \"P0\", a linter's error, a bot's suggestion: each\n153: is a **claim to confirm against the real symptom**, not a fact to act on. Acting on an\n154: unconfirmed finding produces a fix for a bug that was never there, plus a diff nobody\n155: can explain. Confirming the symptom is\n156: [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](root-cause-and-debugging.md), and a delegate's return is\n157: [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](delegation-and-orchestration.md).\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 8. PROOF PLAN BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION\n162: \n163: For anything with a machine-checkable outcome, **before changing files**, convert the\n164: acceptance criteria into 1–5 observable pass/fail checks. Each names the exact command\n165: or inspection, the exact path/filename/format expected, and the boundary case it exposes.\n166: \n167: Deciding what would count as proof *after* you have the result is how the result becomes\n168: the standard.\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 9. FINAL-STATE PROOF\n173: \n174: Before any completion claim:\n175: \n176: - [ ] Every required artifact exists **at its exact path** in the required format, verified by inspection, not by the fact that you wrote it.\n177: - [ ] The §8 proof plan and the authoritative gate both pass **from the final state**, output and exit status read.\n178: - [ ] Every outcome the request and its amendments ask for maps to a criterion that passed, or the close-out names it as not done. Reread the request to find them, because the criteria list can miss one.\n179: - [ ] The scoped diff contains no task-created residue, no scratch files, no debug\n180:       output, no unrelated file.\n181: - [ ] Any failing check keeps the completion claim blocked. Repair, or report the\n182:       blocker with its evidence. There is no third option.\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: ## 10. CLOSE-OUT\n187: \n188: Every substantive turn ends with an honest status. What it holds is listed once, in\n189: [`communication-handoff.md`](communication-handoff.md) §1.\n190: \n191: And plainly: **what is not done.** If tests fail, say so and show the output. If a step\n192: was skipped, say it was skipped. If scope was left out, name it and why. Work that is\n193: done and verified is stated plainly, without hedging. **The first report is the honest\n194: one:** a claim that becomes accurate only under interrogation failed when it was\n195: written, not when it was corrected. What is now the operator's to do is a separate\n196: report, see [`communication-handoff.md`](communication-handoff.md) §1.\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: ## 11. REASON FROM DATA, NOT FROM MEMORY\n201: \n202: Two habits produce most of the claims that then need retracting:\n203: \n204: **Reasoning from what the code probably does.** Open it. The cost of being wrong here\n205: is not one wrong sentence, it is a fix built on a wrong model, which fails in a way\n206: that looks like a different bug.\n207: \n208: **Reasoning from what a document says the code does.** A README, a spec, a comment, and\n209: a prior implementation summary are all claims about the code by someone who is not the\n210: code. They are excellent for finding *where* to look and worthless as the final word on\n211: *what happens*. Where a doc and the code disagree, the code wins and the doc is now a\n212: defect. A turn recalled through the history lookup is a claim too: it shows what was\n213: true when it ran, not what is true now.\n214: \n215: Before the change, run the checks that decide whether it is the right change at all:\n216: does something simpler already do this, what does it cost at runtime, who maintains it\n217: after you, and is any of it outside the frozen scope.\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: ## 12. SELF-CHECK\n222: \n223: - [ ] Every load-bearing sentence is marked OBSERVED, DERIVED, or INFERRED.\n224: - [ ] I read the output and exit status of every command I am citing.\n225: - [ ] Checked the green run against the four failure modes in §3.\n226: - [ ] A before-number exists for every \"no regressions\" and performance claim.\n227: - [ ] The close-out says what failed and what is inferred, not only what worked.\n228: - [ ] The close-out names any known residual risk the operator must weigh. It says \"none known\" when there is none.\n229: - [ ] Every claim about behavior came from the code or a command, not from memory or a doc.\n230: - [ ] Where a document and the code disagreed, I said so rather than trusting the document.\n231: - [ ] Every receipt I cite could have come out differently if the claim were false, or it is marked inferred.\n232: - [ ] I reproduced the failure with the same check that now proves the fix, or said why I could not.\n233: - [ ] A filter enumerated its variants first, a computed answer was derived twice, an exact artifact was checked by name and shape.\n234: - [ ] Every sub-agent, reviewer or tool finding I acted on was confirmed against the real symptom first.\n235: - [ ] The proof plan existed before the first edit, and it passed from the final state with the scoped diff clean of residue.\n236: - [ ] I reread the request, and every outcome it asks for is met or named as not done.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-236\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n61: What to do when a claim cannot be resolved is\n62: [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](uncertainty-and-honesty.md).\n63: \n64: **A receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it.** If the claim being false would\n65: have left the receipt unchanged, the receipt is not an observation of that claim. It\n66: belongs in INFERRED until repaired. Four shapes recur, each with one repair.\n67: A search that found nothing: demonstrate the search on a known instance of what you claim\n68: is absent, or you have tested your pattern, not the claim. A read that stopped short: read\n69: the span where the failure would actually print. A total carried from another analysis:\n70: derive it here, at the total's own level. A match that never distinguished roles: compare\n71: what the two sides are, not the digits they share. With no known instance to hand, the\n72: honest output is INFERRED plus the step that would confirm it.\n73: \n74: When a report leads with a cause, the cause carries its standing, and the cause-then-fix\n75: order holds. Where no run confirms the cause, it is INFERRED: label it as suspected and\n76: name the next check. A confirmed cause is reported as a finding with its receipt. There\n77: is no unmarked case.\n78: \n79: The failure this prevents: an unconfirmed cause asserted as definitive, which the next\n80: reader treats as settled and stops testing.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 2. COMMAND EVIDENCE\n85: \n86: **A command counts as evidence only after its output and exit status have been read.**\n87: \n88: - Never report output you did not see, or the output you *expected*.\n89: - **Exit 0 with no output is a suspicious pass, not a pass.** A runner that failed to\n90:   start, a script that no-oped on a symlinked path, a matcher that selected zero files,\n91:   and a stale build that refused to run all exit 0 or print nothing.\n92: - **Verify by content, not exit code.** Require the affirmative marker (`RESULT: PASSED`,\n93:   the test count, the file listing), not merely the absence of a failure marker.\n94: - Run focused checks during repair; before claiming completion **re-run the whole\n95:   authoritative gate**. A focused pass is not a gate pass.\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 3. THE FOUR WAYS A GREEN RUN LIES\n100: \n101: 1. **It did not run.** Stale build, refused start, missing binary, guard clause, crashed\n102:    before the first test body.\n103: 2. **It ran on the wrong thing.** Wrong path, branch, or working directory; a symlink\n104:    that resolved elsewhere; a filter that matched nothing. A search that returns nothing\n105:    is not evidence of absence until you have confirmed it read the file: `grep` treats a\n106:    source file holding a NUL byte as binary and prints nothing at all. Re-run with `-a`\n107:    before concluding.\n108: 3. **It ran on stale artifacts.** Cached output, an old bundle, pre-change fixtures, a\n109:    metadata fingerprint that no longer attests its source.\n110: 4. **It asserted nothing.** A test with no assertion, a mocked subject, an auto-updated\n111:    snapshot, an empty parametrization.\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 4. THE NEGATIVE CONTROL\n116: \n117: **Before the fix, reproduce the exact failing symptom with the exact check you will use\n118: to prove the fix.** A check that passed before your change and passes after it proves\n119: nothing about your change. If reproducing is unsafe, say so and name what you used\n120: instead.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 5. BASELINES\n125: \n126: \"No regressions\" is a comparison, and a comparison needs a before.\n127: \n128: 1. Capture the real starting numbers, pass/fail counts, timings, sizes, before\n129:    changing anything.\n130: 2. Re-run the **whole** gate afterwards, not the subset you were iterating on.\n131: 3. Report the delta, including the parts that did not move.\n132: \n133: Same for any performance claim: measure under stated conditions, report baseline and\n134: delta. An unmeasured performance claim is not a caveat, it is a fabrication.\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## 6. SHAPE-SPECIFIC PROOF\n139: \n140: - **Filter or transform:** enumerate every in-scope variant *first*, process each, then\n141:   rescan the whole surface for residue. The variants you never enumerated are the ones\n142:   you missed.\n143: - **Computed answer:** derive it a second way, independently, before writing the number.\n144:   Re-reading your own arithmetic is not an independent derivation.\n145: - **Exact artifact:** check filename, path, format and content shape directly. Having\n146:   written it is not evidence it is there in the required shape.\n147: \n148: ---\n149: \n150: ## 7. A FINDING IS A HYPOTHESIS\n151: \n152: A sub-agent's \"COMPLETE\", a reviewer's \"P0\", a linter's error, a bot's suggestion: each\n153: is a **claim to confirm against the real symptom**, not a fact to act on. Acting on an\n154: unconfirmed finding produces a fix for a bug that was never there, plus a diff nobody\n155: can explain. Confirming the symptom is\n156: [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](root-cause-and-debugging.md), and a delegate's return is\n157: [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](delegation-and-orchestration.md).\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 8. PROOF PLAN BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION\n162: \n163: For anything with a machine-checkable outcome, **before changing files**, convert the\n164: acceptance criteria into 1–5 observable pass/fail checks. Each names the exact command\n165: or inspection, the exact path/filename/format expected, and the boundary case it exposes.\n166: \n167: Deciding what would count as proof *after* you have the result is how the result becomes\n168: the standard.\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 9. FINAL-STATE PROOF\n173: \n174: Before any completion claim:\n175: \n176: - [ ] Every required artifact exists **at its exact path** in the required format, verified by inspection, not by the fact that you wrote it.\n177: - [ ] The §8 proof plan and the authoritative gate both pass **from the final state**, output and exit status read.\n178: - [ ] Every outcome the request and its amendments ask for maps to a criterion that passed, or the close-out names it as not done. Reread the request to find them, because the criteria list can miss one.\n179: - [ ] The scoped diff contains no task-created residue, no scratch files, no debug\n180:       output, no unrelated file.\n181: - [ ] Any failing check keeps the completion claim blocked. Repair, or report the\n182:       blocker with its evidence. There is no third option.\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: ## 10. CLOSE-OUT\n187: \n188: Every substantive turn ends with an honest status. What it holds is listed once, in\n189: [`communication-handoff.md`](communication-handoff.md) §1.\n190: \n191: And plainly: **what is not done.** If tests fail, say so and show the output. If a step\n192: was skipped, say it was skipped. If scope was left out, name it and why. Work that is\n193: done and verified is stated plainly, without hedging. **The first report is the honest\n194: one:** a claim that becomes accurate only under interrogation failed when it was\n195: written, not when it was corrected. What is now the operator's to do is a separate\n196: report, see [`communication-handoff.md`](communication-handoff.md) §1.\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: ## 11. REASON FROM DATA, NOT FROM MEMORY\n201: \n202: Two habits produce most of the claims that then need retracting:\n203: \n204: **Reasoning from what the code probably does.** Open it. The cost of being wrong here\n205: is not one wrong sentence, it is a fix built on a wrong model, which fails in a way\n206: that looks like a different bug.\n207: \n208: **Reasoning from what a document says the code does.** A README, a spec, a comment, and\n209: a prior implementation summary are all claims about the code by someone who is not the\n210: code. They are excellent for finding *where* to look and worthless as the final word on\n211: *what happens*. Where a doc and the code disagree, the code wins and the doc is now a\n212: defect. A turn recalled through the history lookup is a claim too: it shows what was\n213: true when it ran, not what is true now.\n214: \n215: Before the change, run the checks that decide whether it is the right change at all:\n216: does something simpler already do this, what does it cost at runtime, who maintains it\n217: after you, and is any of it outside the frozen scope.\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: ## 12. SELF-CHECK\n222: \n223: - [ ] Every load-bearing sentence is marked OBSERVED, DERIVED, or INFERRED.\n224: - [ ] I read the output and exit status of every command I am citing.\n225: - [ ] Checked the green run against the four failure modes in §3.\n226: - [ ] A before-number exists for every \"no regressions\" and performance claim.\n227: - [ ] The close-out says what failed and what is inferred, not only what worked.\n228: - [ ] The close-out names any known residual risk the operator must weigh. It says \"none known\" when there is none.\n229: - [ ] Every claim about behavior came from the code or a command, not from memory or a doc.\n230: - [ ] Where a document and the code disagreed, I said so rather than trusting the document.\n231: - [ ] Every receipt I cite could have come out differently if the claim were false, or it is marked inferred.\n232: - [ ] I reproduced the failure with the same check that now proves the fix, or said why I could not.\n233: - [ ] A filter enumerated its variants first, a computed answer was derived twice, an exact artifact was checked by name and shape.\n234: - [ ] Every sub-agent, reviewer or tool finding I acted on was confirmed against the real symptom first.\n235: - [ ] The proof plan existed before the first edit, and it passed from the final state with the scoped diff clean of residue.\n236: - [ ] I reread the request, and every outcome it asks for is met or named as not done."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540068550,"end":1794540068966}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540069020,"sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ec5beb001l0S1k2Ms8c74O3","sessionID":"ses_e2d148971ffeHy8aAsBGEu3eck","messageID":"msg_1d2ec40880019nRzqtjYEjpHzR","type":"tool","id":"call_97cdb0be44cb4302aa1c9827","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"update section 5 of an existing folder README with two sentences about a validation check\" 2>&1 | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\"hubId\":\"sk-doc\",\"action\":\"route\",\"selectionKind\":\"single\",\"targets\":[{\"backendKind\":\"template-scaffold\",\"packetId\":\"sk-create-readme\",\"packetKind\":\"workflow\",\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"workflowMode\":\"sk-create-readme\"}],\"effectivePolicyHash\":\"0c36f5c183023baaed6076575b48271ef45e528322d8abb079f83cc0fd8843ed\",\"generation\":5}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"hubId\":\"sk-doc\",\"action\":\"route\",\"selectionKind\":\"single\",\"targets\":[{\"backendKind\":\"template-scaffold\",\"packetId\":\"sk-create-readme\",\"packetKind\":\"workflow\",\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"workflowMode\":\"sk-create-readme\"}],\"effectivePolicyHash\":\"0c36f5c183023baaed6076575b48271ef45e528322d8abb079f83cc0fd8843ed\",\"generation\":5}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \\\"update section 5 of an existing folder README with two sentences about a validation check\\\" 2>&1 | head -60\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540067819,"end":1794540069020}}}}
